          "marks": 0.5,
          "negativeMarks": 0.125,
          "explanation": "<p>The correct answer is &#39;<strong>monies</strong>&#39;.</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;\"><img height=\"26px\" src=\"//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png\" width=\"26px\" /><strong><span style=\"vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;\"><u>Key Points</u></span></strong></span></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>&#39;<strong>Monies</strong>&#39; is the plural form of money which means amounts of money.\n\n\t<ul>\n\t\t<li><strong>For eg.-&nbsp; Monies </strong>have been deposited for the charity event.</li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n\t<li>Thus we will use &#39;<strong>monies</strong>&#39; to fill in the blank to complete the sentence meaningfully.</li>\n\t<li>Hence, <strong>option 2</strong> is the correct answer.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p><span style=\"display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;\"><img height=\"26px\" src=\"//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/additional-information-image.png\" width=\"26px\" /><strong><span style=\"vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;\"><u>Additional Information</u></span></strong></span></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li><strong>Penny</strong> is&nbsp;a British bronze coin and monetary unit equal to one-hundredth of a pound.\n\n\t<ul>\n\t\t<li><strong>For eg.-&nbsp;</strong>&nbsp;On the king&#39;s birthday each bedesman received a new blue gown, a loaf, a bottle of ale, and a leathern purse containing a <strong>penny&nbsp;</strong>for every year of the king&#39;s life.</li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n</ul>",
